      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The group has observation notes, participation records, and ideas from a closing discussion.\", \"decision\": \"How should the garden choose its next seasonal priority?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nMembers begin with observation notes and use participation records to choose a feasible priority. The next priority addresses a noticed need within available effort.\nMembers propose a seasonal priority during discussion and check it against both sets of records. A new idea is tested against conditions and available participation.\nMembers begin with participation records and choose an observed need that volunteers can support. The next priority starts from the work capacity the group actually has."
    }
